{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`docs/ticket-model.md:12` currently hand-maintains the ticket taxonomy and says there are five ticket types/statuses. The canonical vocabulary in `src/rebar/types.py:21-23` now defines seven statuses (`idea`, `open`, `in_progress`, `blocked`, `closed`, `archived`, `deleted`) and seven ticket types (`bug`, `epic`, `story`, `task`, `session_log`, `code_review`, `identity`). The relationship prose below that intro is already current, so this ticket is limited to eliminating taxonomy drift while preserving the hand-maintained relationship documentation.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a deterministic generator/checker at `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py` that imports the canonical `TicketType` and `TicketStatus` literals from `src/rebar/types.py`, renders only a clearly marked taxonomy block in `docs/ticket-model.md`, and leaves all prose outside the markers byte-for-byte unchanged. The generated block will replace the stale introductory taxonomy sentence with tables/lists for the canonical type and status vocabularies plus a short note that the relationship sections remain hand-maintained. The script will support a write mode to regenerate the block and a check mode that exits non-zero when `docs/ticket-model.md` is stale after a vocabulary change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/types.py`: read-only source of truth for `TicketType`/`TicketStatus`; tests may monkeypatch or copy a fixture to simulate a vocabulary addition, but the production vocabulary is not changed by this ticket.\n- `docs/ticket-model.md`: receives one marked generated taxonomy section; all relationship/hierarchy/link/tag prose outside the markers must be preserved.\n- `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`: new deterministic generator and drift checker with stable ordering from the canonical literal definitions.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`: held-out oracle coverage for generation, stale-output detection, and simulated source-vocabulary drift.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out TDD will start with unit tests for the generator/checker rather than editing production code first. The oracle covers:\n\n1. Rendering includes all seven live ticket types and all seven live statuses from `src/rebar/types.py:21-23`.\n2. Running the generator against `docs/ticket-model.md` preserves relationship prose outside the marked taxonomy block.\n3. A deliberately stale generated block makes check mode fail and report that regeneration is required.\n4. A deliberate source-vocabulary addition in a copied/monkeypatched `types.py` fixture makes check mode fail when the documentation was not regenerated.\n5. Re-running generation is deterministic/idempotent: a second run produces no diff.\n\nValidation commands: the focused pytest for `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`, the documented script check mode, then the ticket's verify commands (`make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make test` when required by the ticket gate).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` contains a marked generated taxonomy section whose type/status content is derived from the canonical `TicketType` and `TicketStatus` literals in `src/rebar/types.py:21-23`.\n- [ ] The generated taxonomy lists all seven current ticket types and all seven current statuses, including `code_review`, `identity`, `archived`, and `deleted`; verified by `tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`.\n- [ ] Hand-maintained relationship, hierarchy, link, and tag prose outside the generated taxonomy markers is unchanged by regeneration; verified by a preservation test.\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py --check` exits non-zero for both a deliberately stale generated block and a simulated source-vocabulary addition without regeneration.\n- [ ] Generation is deterministic/idempotent: running the write mode twice leaves `docs/ticket-model.md` unchanged on the second run.\n- [ ] The focused generator tests pass and the ticket verify commands pass before the Gerrit change is submitted."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788468580482061644,"uuid":"83f0f6fb-db0a-47f1-80cc-75a1035c0d11"}